From 951324e6bb2cd58d3e9696533b04fac66ec0082c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ferdausfs <178710601+ferdausfs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 07:06:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(push): stop silent Telegram auto-push death (v6.10.1)

Live /health (2026-08-12): pushEnabled=true, subscriberCount=1,
pushesLast24h=0 while the scanner keeps saving tradeable rows
(ADA/USD pending SELL sig_1786517126427 with no pushLog).

Root causes with evidence:
- claimPushLock ran BEFORE sendMessage. A 401/403 held the 30-min
  lock and wrote no pushLog, so every later tick returned 'locked'.
- pushesLast24h counted pushLog:* keys that result-push deletes,
  so a full day of resolve looked like zero deliveries.
- scheduled() wrap-and-return + nested waitUntil(saveAndPush)
  could freeze the isolate after the scan, killing the Telegram send.
- /health only checked !!BOT_TOKEN, so a wrong/whitespace token
  looked "enabled".

Fix: release the lock on send failure; persist lastAttempt + a
durable 24h counter; /health.push exposes enabled, noTokenReason,
tokenValid (getMe), lastAttempt, subscriber snapshot; await the
*/5 scan and awaitPersist from the scanner; harden auto_users
shape and trim BOT_TOKEN.

Tests: fix_tests 302/0 (T43 pins the lock-release + health path),
phase10 19/19 + 71/0, r71 117P/0F, d2/probe/eh/fx/p7 all green.
